title: A failed build/pull/push is still HTTP 200
updated: 2026-08-24T04:20:54Z
---

The engine reports stream failures as errorDetail inside the event stream while the HTTP status stays 200, so _request does not croak and every caller must scan the events itself. Consider a shared helper that inspects a parsed event list and croaks on errorDetail, opt-in per call site so raw event access stays available.
